---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---
<BaseLayout title="Review and Safety Boundaries" description="How BodyWise Lab handles health evidence, reviewer limits, and corrections.">
  <section class="clinical-container py-16 md:py-24">
    <div class="grid gap-8 md:grid-cols-[0.85fr_1.15fr] md:items-end">
      <div>
        <p class="section-kicker">Evidence Review</p>
        <h1 class="section-title mt-3">Review and safety boundaries</h1>
      </div>
      <p class="text-lg leading-8 text-muted-foreground">BodyWise Lab is an editorial health-and-fitness publication, not a clinic. We do not claim personal diagnosis or individualized medical review. Our trust signal is source-checking, conservative safety boundaries, and transparent correction handling.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="mt-12 grid gap-6 md:grid-cols-3">
      <article class="clinical-card p-6"><span class="verified-badge">Source quality</span><h2 class="mt-4 text-2xl font-extrabold text-primary">Primary-source first</h2><p class="mt-4 text-sm leading-7 text-muted-foreground">Articles prioritize CDC, NIH, AHA, ACSM, FDA, Cochrane, PubMed-indexed research, and other official or peer-reviewed sources. We avoid unsupported testimonials as evidence.</p></article>
      <article class="clinical-card p-6"><span class="verified-badge">Medical limits</span><h2 class="mt-4 text-2xl font-extrabold text-primary">No personal care claims</h2><p class="mt-4 text-sm leading-7 text-muted-foreground">Content is general education. It should not be used to diagnose, treat, or override clinician instructions, especially for blood pressure, illness recovery, pregnancy, medications, or supplement interactions.</p></article>
      <article class="clinical-card p-6"><span class="verified-badge">Corrections</span><h2 class="mt-4 text-2xl font-extrabold text-primary">Fixes are logged</h2><p class="mt-4 text-sm leading-7 text-muted-foreground">Readers can report factual errors through the contact page. We re-check the cited source, update the article when needed, and preserve visible update dates.</p></article>
    </div>
    <div class="clinical-card mt-10 p-6"><h2 class="text-2xl font-extrabold text-primary">Why there are no named medical reviewers on every article</h2><p class="mt-3 text-muted-foreground">Named clinical review is shown only when a real reviewer assignment exists. Until then, articles are labeled as editorially source-checked rather than personally medically endorsed.</p><div class="mt-6 flex flex-wrap gap-3"><a href="/editorial-process/" class="btn-secondary">Editorial process</a><a href="/contact/" class="btn-secondary">Report a correction</a></div></div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
